      "title": "Context decay is quietly killing your features before they go live",
      "url": "https://www.thoughtworks.com/insights/blog/continuous-delivery/Context-decay-is-killing-your-features-before-they-go-live",
      "source": "rss",
      "source_name": "Thoughtworks",
      "source_id": "rss:thoughtworks",
      "signal": 4,
      "why_it_matters": "Process warning",
      "summary": "Context decay can significantly hinder the effectiveness of features before they go live, as the knowledge and reasoning behind decisions fade over time. This leads to unnecessary delays and rediscovery of information that was once clear, ultimately impacting deployment efficiency.",
      "key_points": [
        "Delayed releases contribute to cognitive context decay, affecting team memory and decision-making.",
        "Documentation alone cannot capture the reasoning and assumptions behind decisions; timely feedback is crucial.",
        "Shortening release cycles can mitigate context decay and enhance the quality of feedback from real users."
      ],
      "takeaway": "To combat context decay, prioritize shorter release cycles and maintain fresh team context for better decision-making.",
